Z||000004||AusFiero||05-22-2001||09:24 AM||||Heres my version of red and grey.<BR>Recently finished off.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/interior01_3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/interior06_1.jpg"> <P>The sub console and speaker pods are also available for sale. (shameless plug  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P>More pics at <A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||05-22-2001||06:59 PM||||Yeap, ok, thats what I had to do, no question about it now. I am definatly going to do a red/grey interior. I'm going to attempt to cover the dash (spare) in vinyl, probally dark grey. Then the same seats at "T-top Fiero" has. Get matching vinyl for the light grey trim on the seats and cover the center console and all the trim panels in the intior with it. Then have the shifter surround almost like T-top Fiero, except a little lighter, same color as the dash. Radio surround will be in the same light grey as the seats also. All the trim peices will be redone in Carbon fiber, probally black/grey and red. My steering wheel is currently black and red Grant, but I am thinking of getting rid of it and getting a carbon fiber one once the interior is done. Damn I can't wait to get this underway!<P>AusFiero: That car of yours is just absolutly a work of art! I work at a high end stereo shop here, and was going to do my kickpanel and door enclosures myself, but I am wondering how much you sell yours for? I am in need of a door enclosure to hold either a 4" or 6.5", im still playing with imageing. I am going to have 3 way components up front, with a 4" midrange, 6.5" midbass, and 1" tweeter. I am still deciding if I want to put the 4" in the kickpanel or the door. My tweets are going to go in a little custom baffle right where the dash meets the window meets the piller trim. I can fiberglass alright, but I hate doing it. I always end up cutting up too little mat, then removeing my gloves to cut up more only to come back to find I am out yet one more glass jar and paint brush. I hate when that happens. That, and I really hate cleaning up afterwards, but usally the result is worth it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thanks man, that car is the best looking custom interior job Iv ever seen.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||05-22-2001||07:02 PM||||Hey AusFiero, where did you get your carpet? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000007||AusFiero||05-22-2001||08:05 PM||||The speaker pods are available for $67.50 Seanh, insured and delivered to your door in the price. If you have a stereo shop and want more than 5 sets at a time I can do you a better deal as they do fit a lot of cars besids Fieros. First batch will be available for shipping on Thursday, well so my manufacturers are telling me. That lot is already sold out through pre orders.<P>The original thread for the speaker pods is at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007205.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007205.html</A> <P>I have 6" splits in mine. Well in Australia the measure them from the inside rim and call them 5 3/4" for some reason. Well at some shops.<P>The carpet is a wallet biting custom sewn job. Cost me $250, but I certainly do like it a lot more than Pontiacs attempt at deciding which shade of grey to use in the carpet. Hey lets just use em all :P||||reg||1
Z||000008||AusFiero||05-23-2001||03:15 AM||||Oh and thanks for the compliments seanh. It makes it all worthwhile when someone appreciates the time you put into your car.<P>It doesn't cop much appreciation in AUS because most Pontiac owners in our car club don't know anything about Fieros and snub them. <P>A good example was my loss at the Pontiac nationals. Got marked down in the Fiero class (standard) because of my interior and narrowly lost at best Fiero. Car that won had a local Commodore dash, SAAS seats and a bloody Holden engine it. It was also a non original colour. Yet it was judged more original than my near dead stock Fiero with a recoloured interior. They marked me down big time for the sub woofer. Go figure hey.<P>The to make things worse the D***head judges didn't even judge it for best custom interior even though they deemed it non stock. That class it may won as an 8 year old black vinyl interior won, neat but no where near the work of mine. Even the owner of that car was shocked he won the class as there was at least 7 better interiors<P>Us poor Fiero owners really do cop it in car shows that are non Fiero related, which is all of them here.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
